        // and sets Acc[actor].unlockTime to at least block.timestamp (since Put sets to max(_unlockTime, block.timestamp)).
        // The mutant returns early on msg.value==0 and therefore does not update the log/unlockTime.
        // We assert that the last log sender equals the caller (actor). This holds for the reference for ALL inputs,
        // and the mutant breaks it for at least some input (when msg.value==0).

        // Read Log.LastMsg via the public Log contract getter: Log is accessible through C.LogFile public variable's History or LastMsg is internal but Log exposes History; however in the provided C the Log contract has public array History and LastMsg (not public). We can observe via History[History.length-1].Sender.
